<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6822"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 11:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To Lctrip / Toasties in rural drop <BR> <BR>You mentiomed the Chinese New Year &#40;Year of the Rooster&#41;, as did Nancydrew above, as did Aaron Brown on CNN &#40;9pm CST&#41; this evening. At the end of his program each night, a rooster crows and he shows the newspaper &#39;headlines&#39; from several prominant newspapers that will appear the &#39;following morning&#39;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
